<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Sungei Way plans &quot;Sunken City&quot;.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Sungei Way plans &quot;Sunken City&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian construction and theme park company Sungei Way Holdings Bhd said it plans to build a three billion ringgit &quot;underground city&quot; in the Malaysian capital.</p>
<p>The new development, to be called the Sunken City, will be located near the company's Sunway Lagoon theme park, Sungei Way's president Jeffrey Cheah told reporters on Friday.</p>
<p>It will be built 50 metres (yards) below ground and will include a hotel, a shopping centre and parks, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The construction of the city, which will begin at the end of this year, is expected to be completed within the next five years,&quot; Cheah said</p>
<p>The complex will be linked with the nearest railway station by a 15-km monorail system, he said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 201 4813)</p>
